{number: 62}
{title: Saved by Grace}
{key: F}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[F] Some day the silver cord will break,
And I no more as [C7] now shall sing;
But [F] oh, the joy when I shall wake
Within the [C7] palace of the [F] King!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
And I shall [Bb] see Him face to [F] face,
And tell the [C7] story—Saved by [F] grace;
And I shall [Bb] see Him face to [F] face,
And tell the [C7] story—Saved by [F] grace.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[F] Some day my earthly house will fall,
I cannot tell how [C7] soon ’twill be;
But [F] this I know-—my All in All
Has now a [C7] place in heav’n for [F] me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[F] Some day, when fades the golden sun
Beneath the rosy-[C7] tinted west,
My [F] blessed Lord will say, “Well done!”
And I shall [C7] enter into [F] rest.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[F] Some day: till then I’ll watch and wait,
My lamp all trimmed and [C7] burning bright,
That [F] when my Saviour opens the gate,
My soul to [C7] Him may take its [F] flight.
{end_of_verse}
